    shortDescription: "List the pros and cons.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nAdvantages: independent scaling, technology diversity, faster deployment, resilience, and team autonomy. Disadvantages: complexity, network latency, distributed transactions, increased operational overhead, and debugging challenges.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks engineering judgment around what are the advantages and disadvantages of microservices. A useful answer makes the benefit, cost, and condition for choosing the approach explicit.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Advantages: independent scaling, technology diversity, faster deployment, resilience, and team autonomy.\n2. Disadvantages: complexity, network latency, distributed transactions, increased operational overhead, and debugging challenges.\n3. Connect the concept to latency, failure modes, capacity, consistency, and operational cost rather than discussing components in isolation..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nStart with why an engineer would want the approach, then cover the operational or design cost that comes with it.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. Advantages: independent scaling, technology diversity, faster deployment, resilience, and team autonomy.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production platform, what are the advantages and disadvantages of microservices affects component boundaries, capacity, latency, consistency, or failure handling. The design should start from traffic and reliability assumptions, then choose the simplest architecture that meets them.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Listing benefits and drawbacks without saying when they matter.\n- Treating one approach as universally superior.\n- Ignoring operational cost, maintenance, or failure behavior.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nName the constraint that makes the trade-off acceptable, then state when you would deliberately choose another approach.",
