    question: "What is the Difference between circuit breaker and bulkhead?",
    slug: "circuit-breaker-vs-bulkhead",
    shortDescription: "Compare the patterns.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nCircuit breaker prevents repeated calls to a failing service. Bulkhead isolates resources (e.g., thread pools) to prevent failure in one part from affecting others. They are complementary.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe interviewer is checking whether you can explain the boundary between the two choices in what is the difference between circuit breaker and bulkhead and tie that difference to an engineering decision.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Circuit breaker prevents repeated calls to a failing service.\n2. Bulkhead isolates resources (e.g., thread pools) to prevent failure in one part from affecting others.\n3. They are complementary.\n4. Connect the concept to latency, failure modes, capacity, consistency, and operational cost rather than discussing components in isolation..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nFocus on the difference that changes the engineering decision rather than comparing every feature. Use one scenario to make it concrete.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, choose the option whose behavior matches the requirement and compare the resulting operational consequence. Circuit breaker prevents repeated calls to a failing service.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. Circuit breaker prevents repeated calls to a failing service.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Defining both sides but never stating the practical difference.\n- Choosing one option without naming the requirement that drives the choice.\n- Treating platform-specific behavior as a universal rule.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nState the decision rule early: when would you choose A, and when would you choose B? That is more useful than listing every secondary difference.",
