    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nServer Components are React components that run only on the server, not in the browser. They can be async and directly access backend resources. They reduce client-side JavaScript and improve performance. The App Router uses them by default.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks breadth, but the useful signal is whether you can explain what the important items are for and distinguish the ones that are commonly confused.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Server Components are React components that run only on the server, not in the browser.\n2. They can be async and directly access backend resources.\n3. They reduce client-side JavaScript and improve performance.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nAnswer the requested list directly, then go deeper on the item most relevant to the interviewer’s context.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. Server Components are React components that run only on the server, not in the browser.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. Server Components are React components that run only on the server, not in the browser.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Reciting names without explaining their purpose.\n- Missing the common options while focusing on obscure variants.\n- Giving an exhaustive list when the question only asks for the important examples.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nGive the common answers first and attach one useful distinction or use case to each instead of reciting a long list.",
